          <p>
            A treadmill had to clear four bars. <strong>A stated capacity of 350 lb or more.</strong>
            <strong>A stated top speed of at least 10 mph</strong>; all six reach 12. <strong>A named brand
            with a storefront or support line</strong>, which removed dozens of unbranded listings, including
            a 400 lb, 12 mph machine whose brand field reads "Generic". And <strong>a clear statement of belt
            size</strong>, because deck length is the figure that decides whether a treadmill suits running
            at all.
          </p>
          <p>
            We also kept away from the picks on our two neighbouring pages where we could. The Sole F65,
            NordicTrack Commercial 1750 and 2450, Life Fitness T3 and <a href="/matrix-fitness-t7xe-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Matrix T7xe</a> are covered on our heavy
            people page, and the Spirit XT485, Horizon 7.4 AT, ECHANFIT and WELLFIT machines on the <a href="/best-treadmills-for-heavy-people/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best heavy-duty treadmills</a> page. Several of them are good choices for a heavy runner too; this page is more useful if it
